
== exact quotients ==
6d / 2d                            3
1d / 2d                            0.5
1d / 8d                            0.125
10d / 4d                           2.5
100d / 0.5d                        200
9d / 3d                            3
-1d / 4d                           -0.25
1d / -4d                           -0.25
-1d / -4d                          0.25

== preferred scale keeps what the operands had ==
1.0d / 2d                          0.5
1.00d / 2d                         0.50
1.000d / 2d                        0.500
7.50d / 2.5d                       3.0
1.50d / 0.5d                       3.0
2.50d / 1.25d                      2
12.5d / 0.25d                      50
0.00d / 5d                         0.00
0d / 5d                            0

== quotients that do not terminate ==
1d / 3d                            0.3333333333333333333
2d / 3d                            0.6666666666666666667
-1d / 3d                           -0.3333333333333333333
1d / 7d                            0.1428571428571428571
100d / 3d                          33.33333333333333333
0.5d / 3d                          0.1666666666666666667
1.000d / 3d                        0.3333333333333333333
22d / 7d                           3.142857142857142857
123456789.123456789d / 7d          17636684.160493827
1d / 9223372036854775807d          0.0000000000000000001084202172

== remainder takes the sign of the dividend ==
7d % 3d                            1
-7d % 3d                           -1
7d % -3d                           1
-7d % -3d                          -1
7.5d % 2d                          1.5
5.25d % 0.5d                       0.25
5d % 0.50d (scale 2)               0.00
10d % 5d                           0
0.3d % 0.1d (exact, unlike 0.3 % 0.1) 0.0
number: 0.3 % 0.1                  0.09999999999999998

== division and remainder go together ==
17.5d / 4d (truncated)             4
17.5d % 4d                         1.5
q * b + r == a                     true

== function forms ==
decimal.div(10d, 4d)               2.5
decimal.rem(10d, 4d)               2
decimal.div(1i, 8i)                0.125

== division by zero ==
1d / 0d                            error: decimal division by zero
0d / 0d                            error: decimal division by zero
1d % 0d                            error: decimal division by zero
1d / 0.00d                         error: decimal division by zero
decimal.div(1d, 0d)                error: decimal division by zero

== not defined ==
5d // 2d                           error: attempt to perform arithmetic (idiv) on decimal
2d ^ 3d                            error: attempt to perform arithmetic (pow) on decimal
use trunc for a floor-style quotient 2
